## COMPREHENSIVE SECURITY AUDIT REPORT: Claude Hub App

Based on my thorough analysis of the codebase, here's a detailed security and functionality audit of all write operations:

---

### EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

The Claude Hub app has **CRITICAL path traversal vulnerabilities** and several missing safety checks in file write operations. While the base64url encoding of project IDs provides some protection, agent/command/rule names are NOT validated and can be weaponized to write files outside intended directories. Additionally, **commands and rules cannot be created/edited from the UI** - only read.

---

## CRITICAL ISSUES

### 1. PATH TRAVERSAL VULNERABILITY (HIGH SEVERITY)

**Location**: `src/server.js` - All write endpoints that accept `name` parameter

**Vulnerable Code**:
```javascript
// Lines 174-180: PUT /api/global/agents/:name
app.put('/api/global/agents/:name', (req, res) => {
  const dir = path.join(CLAUDE_DIR, 'agents');
  ensureDir(dir);
  const filePath = path.join(dir, req.params.name + '.md');  // NO SANITIZATION!
  fs.writeFileSync(filePath, req.body.content);
  res.json({ ok: true, agent: parseAgent(filePath) });
});
```

**The Attack**:
```
PUT /api/global/agents/../../../../../../etc/passwd
PUT /api/global/agents/../../../../../../../tmp/malicious.md
PUT /api/projects/[projectId]/agents/../../../config.json
```

An attacker could write arbitrary files anywhere the Node.js process has permissions because `req.params.name` is never validated. The `path.join()` call does **NOT** prevent path traversal when `..` is used.

**Proof of Concept**:
- Request: `PUT /api/global/agents/../../etc/passwd` with content "malicious"
- Result: Would write to `/home/user/.claude/agents/../../etc/passwd` → resolves to `/home/user/etc/passwd` or higher depending on path

**Affected Endpoints**:
- `PUT /api/global/agents/:name` (line 174)
- `DELETE /api/global/agents/:name` (line 182)
- `PUT /api/projects/:id/agents/:name` (line 222)
- `DELETE /api/projects/:id/agents/:name` (line 231)
- `PUT /api/projects/:id/commands/:name` (line 256)
- `POST /api/move-agent` (line 431) - agentName not validated
- `POST /api/copy-agent` (line 465) - agentName not validated

**Frontend Context**:
The frontend creates agent names like:
```typescript
const slug = newName.trim().toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, '-')
```
This replaces spaces with hyphens but does NOT prevent `../` sequences. A user could type "my agent/../../../etc/passwd" and the frontend would send exactly that.

**Fix Required**:
```javascript
function validateName(name) {
  // Reject any path components
  if (name.includes('/') || name.includes('\\') || name.includes('..')) {
    throw new Error('Invalid name: contains path separators');
  }
  // Only allow alphanumeric, hyphens, underscores
  if (!/^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/.test(name)) {
    throw new Error('Invalid name: contains invalid characters');
  }
  return name;
}
```

